<http://purl.org/spar/bido/journal-impact-factor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A measure reflecting the average number of citations to recent articles published in the journal. It is frequently used as a proxy for the relative importance of a journal within its field, with journals with higher impact factors deemed to be more important than those with lower ones." .
